<<PlayBackgroundMusic Emotional_1>>
<<SetBGSprite "HutInterior">>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Today I change seats, Captain—till now I drove the bus, but from here I ring the bell and keep time while Uncle Dev takes the wheel inside the nets.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: If you change seats, will I still hear you?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Not over his voice, but between it—like the space in a drumbeat where habits live.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: What if he moves my feet different or changes my grip? We did it one way for months.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Then you try his way first—no arguing inside the net, just try, feel, and file it. After practice we ask why together, because learning looks clumsy before it looks clever.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: So… try now, ask later.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Exactly. Three permissions before we step forward—one: look ordinary while learning something extraordinary; two: ask questions that sound silly but save time; three: disappoint me for one session if it means you did the right thing slowly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I accept.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: And three promises I want back.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: School stays first—numbers don't drop because nets are exciting. Two: manners louder than talent, no throwing, showing off, or shrinking. Three: health over heroics—if something hurts, you speak.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I promise. What about you?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: My turn.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: One: I won't coach over Uncle Dev—my mouth will be in my pocket, my eyes on your effort. Two: I'll be there early, steady, and boring in the best way, and three: I'll keep home soft and honest with warmth, water, and work waiting whether you win or wobble.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Anxious">>
Raju: I'm excited but also a little scared—with you I know the answers, but with him I'll be asked new ones.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: New questions mean new rooms—we're opening doors, not breaking walls. If doubt knocks, say your name once and check your anchor: the rusty nail, the breath you count, the thread on your wrist—you're not alone, just growing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Bhai… who am I when I walk in there?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Many things in this order—student, teammate, worker. The applause can join the line at the end—walk like work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Will you clap if I do something right?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: I'll clap in my chest—outside I'll be a quiet yes. Let Dev-sir measure while I count effort.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: And if I miss?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: We've practiced missing with manners—you already know that dance of bowing to it, learning, and moving.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Bhai, thank you for the mornings—for the towel, the tape, the brick sanding, and for calling me captain when I was only learning to stand.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Sad">>
Ramu: Thank you for showing up when sleeping was easier, for keeping the bat face up and your promises the same, and for letting me be your first coach.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: You'll always be my first coach.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Sad">>
Ramu: And always your brother after that. If the ground ever makes you feel small, remember the lane made you tall.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Can I—

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Sad">>
Ramu: Come here.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: I'll make you proud, but not noisy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Make yourself honest—pride will find us if it needs to. Alright, little-big man, bat face-up for a breath, pocket your pencil, lift your eyes, and walk your work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Reporting.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Through here. When you look back, I'll be right where you left me—light on, mouth shut, heart loud.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Lighthouse.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Captain.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
<<EndEvent>>
